# Conformance probe pack for value transforms (spec 0.15) on the `json` wire.
# Public. No kinds. `iscale` reads a number's text as an exact decimal and
# writes the exact quotient: seconds with a fraction to `time_ms`
# (iscale:1000), digits beyond 2^53 kept as written (ruling 7), thirds of a
# unit with an offset, whose quotient may not terminate. `scale` computes in
# doubles and never rounds (ruling 8): an integer of 1e-7 degrees to degrees,
# a factor of 10 that overflows, an offset. The plain members name the keys
# of the `bits` packs of this version, for conversions to and from them. The
# group `items` is there for ruling 27: a number no field reads, in a group
# item or anywhere else, outside the double range is `malformed-wire`.
format  conformance-transforms-json
version 0.15.0
distribution public
source  "goat-transformers spec/engine-spec.md (synthetic probe format, no external standard)"
uses    probe
wire    json
field   time_ms       sec    iscale:1000
field   probe.big     big    iscale:1
field   probe.thirds  th     iscale:3:1
field   lat           lat    scale:1/10000000
field   ce            ce     scale:10
field   course        crs    scale:1/100:180
field   probe.n       n      int
field   probe.x       x      int
field   probe.y       y      int
field   probe.z       z      int
field   probe.w       w      int
field   probe.c1      c1     int
field   probe.c2      c2     int
field   probe.ratio   ratio  float
field   probe.a       a      float
field   hae           hae    float
field   probe.label   label  string
field   probe.s2      s2     string
field   probe.tag     tag    string
field   probe.s1      s1     string
field   callsign      cs     string
field   uid           id     string
field   probe.val     val    int
group   probe.items   items
  field  probe.qty  q  int
end
